WEBVTT

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.590
Yuzuki!

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.190
Please, listen to me!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.190
Wait!

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.530
I'll make you a promise!

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.830
In a week,
we're going to shoot fireworks over the lake!

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.250
Yuzuki!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.560
You'll need some help, right?

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.580
Here are those phonebooks.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.140
Wow, thanks!

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.840
I thought you might need a few for the areas outside Kiriyako as well.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.290
Also, feel free to use our phone.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.450
Thank you!

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.910
Nonsense, I should be thanking you.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.070
Huh?

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:32.920
I had given up thinking there was anything I could do to help Yuzuki.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.850
Koharu...

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.660
So you have my thanks!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:11.750
I see.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.950
I really appreciate it!

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.130
Well, I guess it's fine.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.580
Sorry for taking up all your time today.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.620
Don't worry about it.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.280
I don't want to give up halfway.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.770
Koharu...

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:50.300
I really hope we get the permission to shoot off those fireworks.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.040
Yeah.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.920
Yuzuki, your door's open.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.790
She's not home?

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.260
Damn it!

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.300
Got a minute?

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.220
Yuzuki!

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.310
Listen to me!

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:55.710
Yuzuki!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:00.920
What?

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.330
You said you wanted to talk? Hurry up then.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.280
Unlike you, I'm a very busy person—

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.650
You need to stop all this.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.590
No matter what you do,
the Disc won't just disappear.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.400
Komiya's really putting her heart into this, too.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.300
Huh?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.680
She's pushing for the fireworks display.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.970
Even Koharu's helping her.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:21.110
I bet you went and—

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.640
That has nothing to do with me!

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.980
Sorry.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.230
My apologies.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.400
What?

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.190
You've held a grudge against me all this time, haven't you?

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.950
I didn't listen to what you said back then, and...

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.030
Why?

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:42.760
I'm sorry about that.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.540
Why?

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:43.910
So—

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.820
Why are <i>you</i> apologizing?!

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:46.670
Stupid Souta!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.560
H-Hey!

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:50.670
Yuzuki...

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.060
It looks like it's just not happening with the Disc up there...

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.950
There's still time.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.550
Let's come back to ask them again!

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.570
Yup, of course.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:19.570
Nonoka!

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:21.080
Noel!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.960
Nonoka!

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.270
Hamburger steak!

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.440
Of course.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.420
Fireworks? We're going to have fireworks?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.590
Hopefully. We still need permission.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:39.300
Fireworks!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.300
Hey, Nonoka?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.200
Yes?

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.590
What are "fireworks?"

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.360
What?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.470
Thanks for the food!

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.440
So yummy!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.300
Fireworks are things that shoot high into the sky,

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.190
and then,

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:57.090
boom!

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.360
"Boom?"

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:00.990
Whizz...

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:02.970
Bang!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:05.580
Noel?!

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.830
Wow! So these are fireworks!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:11.930
Yup.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:13.840
This is from the festival, seven years ago.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.840
Fireworks were shot above the lake.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.590
It's sparkly and so pretty!

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.660
Whizz!

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.950
Bang!

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:26.220
Sparkle, sparkle!

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.350
Just like that?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.730
Yep, exactly.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:32.880
Noel,

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.410
If you'd like, I can lend that album to you.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.790
Really?

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.990
Just this once.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:41.660
Yay!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.470
Thanks, Nonoka!

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.870
Noel!
Thanks, Nonoka!

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.050
That's dangerous!

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:46.250
Ow!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.060
What are you doing, Koharu?

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:51.750
Come and have dinner.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.670
Um, Yuzuki?

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.700
See you tomorrow then.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:48.680
Give it up already!

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.280
There's no way you'll be able to organize a fireworks show in less than a week!

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.200
I'm not giving up.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.000
Why not?

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.280
The Disc is still here!

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.440
It's impossible!

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.680
Because I promised!

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:04.950
Y-You didn't mean that!

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.200
What are the fireworks to you?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.160
Do you think seeing fireworks will make me happy or something?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.510
No.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:19.140
At first, I felt that I wanted you to see them,

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.050
but that's not it now.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:22.710
Huh?

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.850
<i>I</i> want to see the fireworks.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.220
Just like we did together when we were kids.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:34.070
Wh-What?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.410
You don't mean any of that.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.730
Yuzuki!

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.940
Yuzuki, let's get going!

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.510
We promised everyone.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.540
Okay.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.330
Yuzuki?

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.280
Yuzuki, where are you?

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:15.690
Yuzuki!

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.890
Souta!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.310
Souta, where are you?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.900
Souta!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.910
It's tomorrow, isn't it?

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:33.900
Eh?

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.610
Are you coming too, Togawa-san?

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.220
I'll come.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:45.110
If the fireworks actually happen, I mean.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:49.590
Make sure you come!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:53.870
Yuzuki?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.810
I need to talk to you.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.560
You're...

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:11.510
Noel?

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:22.750
I was beginning to think you'd never talk to me again.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.960
Is that why you're with Nonoka all the time now?

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.840
No, that's not it.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:32.260
We were always together back then—

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.380
You're wrong!

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:35.720
Nonoka doesn't remember anything from seven years ago!

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.810
She doesn't know anything,
but she still says she wants to have fireworks?

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:40.140
She's so insensitive!

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:50.400
Yuzuki, I'm sure that Nonoka wasn't making fun of what you're doing.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.620
What's the real reason you wanted to talk to me?

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:58.660
I...

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.590
This is yummy!

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.420
I wonder if Nonoka will make it for me?

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.680
I've been wondering for a while now,

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.010
but what's your relationship with Nonoka?

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:19.260
Hm? Relationship?

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:22.520
I'm asking how the two of you know each other.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:25.650
She taught me a song one snowy day!

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:27.770
What?

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:29.270
I'll sing it to you!

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.320
Stop.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.450
Don't lie to me.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:42.540
It hasn't snowed since Nonoka came back to this town.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:45.290
Shione, you know a lot about Nonoka!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.750
You're really good friends with her!

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.540
No, I'm not.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.510
Why aren't you anymore?

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.470
Because Nonoka's nothing but a liar.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.260
A huge liar.

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:02.220
Let's eat this together!

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:05.480
You'll feel really happy when you eat something really nice!

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.980
I...

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.030
Why did you go off into the night without telling anyone?

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.790
I dunno. I just felt like it.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.960
Blame me for going and hurting myself.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.460
No, it's not.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.920
That's not true.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:37.590
You should blame...

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:41.930
Yuzuki?

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.270
It's nothing!

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:45.520
Yuzuki!

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.420
Nonoka, are you all right?

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:19.550
Yeah.

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:22.350
Sorry I had to get you involved and everything.

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:24.680
I have faith in you.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:25.430
Huh?

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:30.690
You just need to stick to what you believe no matter what.

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:34.440
Thanks, Koharu!

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:44.990
Oh, it's you again?

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:46.450
Sorry, but I'm afraid I can't—

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:49.710
I'm here for a different request today!

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:18.740
I remembered something! I have to go!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.650
What is it?

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:25.160
I promised all my friends that I'd meet them at the wharf once the fireworks starts!

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.910
Can I go to see them, Mom?

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:29.000
Of course.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.290
But before you do...

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.210
Thank you very much.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:37.920
I'm gonna go now!

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.170
All right, take care.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.640
Koharu, we're going to be very busy tonight.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:51.060
Don't run off to the festival, okay?

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.350
Okay.

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:02.150
Koharu!

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.160
Sorry I... took so long.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:06.910
Koharu!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:08.450
Eh?

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:09.410
Give it here.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:11.830
You came!

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:12.750
Yeah, but...

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:15.580
I dunno if Yuzuki will too.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:18.210
It's up to her.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.000
Yup.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.840
Thanks, Souta.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.630
So, what's the plan?

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:30.720
I thought as much.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.230
You're such a liar.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.030
I wish I could go...

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.790
You're not going?

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:55.500
When there won't even be any fireworks?

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:00.260
Oh, sorry. It's not something you should worry about, Noel.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.050
Don't say that!

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:04.550
Noel's happy when everyone else is happy!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.260
Don't you feel the same, Yuzuki?

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:10.510
Look!

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:13.680
Nonoka's super happy in this!

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.290
This is...

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.410
I see.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.670
She hadn't forgotten.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:40.840
What's wrong, Yuzuki?

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:42.920
Hey, Noel.

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:47.930
Am I "happy"?

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.180
Yup!

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:55.640
Thanks!

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:04.940
Onii-chan!

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.410
Onii-chan?

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.460
Onii-chan!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.430
You sure took your time.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.940
I...

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.350
Yuzuki, I'm sorry.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.190
I couldn't keep my promise about the fireworks.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.860
No...

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.700
I'm the one...

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:34.120
Yuzuki?

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.660
I'm sorry!

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.200
I'm so sorry!

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.120
I've always wanted to say sorry!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.710
To Nonoka, and Koharu, and to you, Onii-chan!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.790
I'm so sorry!

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:49.710
It was all my fault!

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:54.720
I'm sorry!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:58.720
I'm sorry!

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:07.230
After all that, all we have are these sparklers I brought?

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:08.650
Shush!

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:12.990
All of mine were too damp to use after seven years.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:14.610
Suck it up!

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:19.740
I wish Togawa-san had come, too.

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:23.290
Playing with sparklers is fun!

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.960
Whizz...

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:25.880
It is!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:26.630
Whizz...

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:28.420
Bang!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.350
Look, look!

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:55.320
It's so...

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:58.870
So...

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:34.360
Next time, on Sora no Method:

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:35.890
"True Friends."

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:37.220
Look forward to it!
